{"name":"Beef Bourguignon","hex":"#b64701","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beef bourguignon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A French stew dish, consisting of beef, red wine, garlic and vegetables."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beef_bourguignon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beef bourguignon","blocks":[{"text":"Beef bourguignon or bœuf bourguignon, is a French stew of beef braised in red wine, often red Burgundy, and beef stock, typically flavored with carrots, onions, garlic, and a bouquet garni, and garnished with pearl onions and mushrooms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Beef_bourguignon_NYT.jpg/330px-Beef_bourguignon_NYT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beef_bourguignon","wikidata":"Q1022124"},{"title":"Beef","blocks":[{"text":"Beef is the culinary name for meat from cattle. Beef can be prepared in various ways; cuts are often used for steak, which can be cooked to varying degrees of doneness, while trimmings are often ground or minced, as found in most hamburgers. Beef contains protein, iron, and vitamin B12. Along with other kinds of red meat, high consumption is associated with an increased risk of colorectal cancer and cardiovascular disease, especially when processed. Beef has a high environmental impact, being a primary driver of deforestation with the highest greenhouse gas emissions of any agricultural product."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Standing-rib-roast.jpg/330px-Standing-rib-roast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beef","wikidata":"Q192628"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Julia_Child%27s_Boeuf_Bourguignon.jpg/500px-Julia_Child%27s_Boeuf_Bourguignon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x